 Day 25 – Basics of SQL
 What is SQL?

SQL (Structured Query Language) is used to:
Create databases
Store and retrieve data
Manage application backends
SQL is the backbone of most web applications.

 Topics Covered :
Creating databases
Viewing available databases
Selecting a database
Understanding SQL execution flow

 Basic SQL Commands Learned
-- Create a database
CREATE DATABASE cyber_db;

-- Show all databases
SHOW DATABASES;

-- Use a database
USE cyber_db;
Secure Practice :
CREATE DATABASE IF NOT EXISTS cyber_db;

✔ Prevents duplicate errors
✔ Safe execution practice

 Cybersecurity Insight (Day 25)
Databases store sensitive user data
Poor SQL practices can lead to SQL Injection

Secure database design is the first defense layer
